			<div class="content" id="post-content-4849673">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> SCP-#### “The Predatory Tattoo” is an entity in the form of a tattoo usually appearing to look like various predatory creatures. It primarily targets individuals with various tattoos but will on rare occasions appear on individuals with little to no tattoos. A minor memetic effect caused the host prey to retain false memories of receiving the tattoo at some point. As time goes on the victim will notice slight imperfections with the tattoo, such as movement and its eyes seeming to be staring. More tattoos seem to manifest on the host taking on the appearance of bites and claw marks. Eventually after some time has passed the prey host will collapse, dead from unknown causes.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The anomalous entity would first be discovered after a string of mysterious deaths was brought to the attention of the foundation. Investigations of the coroner’s reports on the latest victims showed no outer wounds but upon autopsy revealed several missing organs and parts of muscle tissue. Agents disguised as Federal agents confiscate the most recent body as well as all files on previous victims. After transferring the corpse to a foundation facility, one of the retrieval agents would discover a tattoo of unknown origin on his back after feeling a stinging sensation and seeing the scp taking the form of extinct species of Kaprosuchus as well as a few dozen tatto-like claw marks surrounding the main tattoo. Upon discovering the entity, the Agent willingly accepted being contained, examined and observed to determine the entities capabilities. After the agents death from the scp, the skin of the agents back was removed, preserved and placed in a frame with the scp still in place with physical contact being heavily restricted to prevent containment breaches.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> it has two primary ways of transferring to a new prey host, either by direct touching of the current area it is inhabiting or by viewing the scp for a certain amount of time however these depend on several factors the primary being if it had recently fed and the ability to transfer can be prevented via two way mirrors in its containment cell. It would favor more exotic creatures such as extinct species of predatory creatures in order to attract the attention of tattoo enthusiasts and thus gaining possible new prey hosts. Its main way of hunting would appear to try and make its prey paranoid all the while it toys with its prey.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> As stated, normal means one would take to remove a tattoo does not seem to work with the person attempting to remove the entity reporting feeling unnerved and/or receiving tattooed markings in the form of self defensive slashes or bites.</p>

