<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there MisterNightmare013. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-crit</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Unfortunately, I’m not sure I completely understand how your scp functions at the moment. So it’s a predatory tattoo that “appears” on random people’s skin? Why wouldn’t the victim automatically be suspicious of its appearance?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Claw mark-like tattoos over existing tattoos/bare skin that seem to sting as would normal claw marks would also appear.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What does this mean? Perhaps you should clarify your wording.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Eventually it would kill its victim in the way the predator its based off would normally kill its prey (bruises associated with being constricted being tattooed on the victim or gashes from claws as well)</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Similarly for this statement. How exactly does a victim die? More importantly, <em>why</em> is this happening to victims? How/when does the tattoo appear or choose its victims? There are also sections of your central narrative that jump about and don’t make sense, mainly:</p>
<p>- why would the Foundation investigate a random string of murders? What made them anomalous to begin with?<br />
- why is the Foundation agent sensing a stinging sensation?<br />
- “the form of extinct species of Kaprosuchu” what’s the relevance of this?<br />
- “the Agent willingly accepted being contained and observed to determine the entities behavior.” I’d think the Foundation would conduct more than just observations if they discovered the entity was a tattoo.<br />
- “Its main way of hunting would appear to try and make its prey paranoid all the while it toys with its prey.” I still don’t understand how this would work. Perhaps you could give a specific, detail example.</p>
<p>The concept itself sounds cool, but I have a feeling you have not fleshed out the exact mechanics of your proposed scip. As a result, its anomalous properties sound random / too fantastical and as a result, I can’t really imagine the scp as realistically working.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p>If you decide to revise the concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll take another look. Best of luck!</p>

